.TH REGOLITH-CONVERT-TO-DEBIAN 8 "November 2026" "Regolith" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
regolith-convert-to-debian \- move a Regolith system from Ubuntu 26.04 to Debian forky
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B regolith-convert-to-debian
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B regolith-convert-to-debian
converts the machine it runs on from Ubuntu 26.04 to Debian forky in one run,
keeping Regolith installed from Regolith's Debian archive.
.PP
The Ubuntu package sources are replaced by
.IR /etc/apt/sources.list.d/debian.sources .
Regolith sources move to the Regolith Debian archive of the same stage
.RB ( testing
or
.BR unstable ).
Other sources are disabled where they are: deb822 entries get
.BR "Enabled: no" ,
one-line entries are commented out.
The original files below
.I /etc/apt
are kept in
.IR /var/backups/regolith-convert-to-debian/apt .
.PP
Every installed package then moves to the version the Debian and Regolith
archives provide. Ubuntu packages that Debian provides under another name are
replaced (the coreutils variants, the generic kernel metapackages,
.BR linux-firmware );
Ubuntu packages without a Debian version are removed, except packages
installed from a third-party archive that Debian does not provide, and the
packages of the running kernel, which stay as a fallback until the Debian
kernel has booted. Unmodified configuration files that no installed package
ships any more are deleted; modified ones are kept.
Finally
.I /etc/os-release
and the dpkg origin are switched to Debian.
.PP
The program prints one line for each package it keeps, removes or replaces,
for each source file it disables, and for each modified obsolete
configuration file it keeps, then asks for confirmation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-debian\-mirror " URL"
Debian archive to use. Default:
.IR http://deb.debian.org/debian .
.TP
.BI \-\-debian\-keyring " FILE"
Keyring that signs the Debian archive. Default:
.IR /usr/share/keyrings/debian-archive-keyring.gpg .
.TP
.BI \-\-regolith\-mirror " URL"
Regolith archive to use. Default:
.IR https://archive.regolith-desktop.com .
.TP
.BI \-\-regolith\-stage " STAGE"
Regolith stage to use on Debian,
.B testing
or
.BR unstable .
Needed when the Regolith sources use another stage, such as
.BR stable .
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Do not ask for confirmation. Without it, standard input must be a terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Print what would change and stop. Only the package lists below
.I /var/lib/apt/lists
may be refreshed.
.TP
.B \-\-resume
Finish a conversion that stopped while packages were changing.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a summary of the options and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The conversion, or the dry run, completed.
.TP
.B 2
The program declined to start (not root, not Ubuntu 26.04, held or broken
packages, the default Debian keyring missing, a usage error, or an earlier run
that has to be resumed). Nothing was changed.
.TP
.B 3
A failure before any package changed, such as an unreachable archive, a bad
signature or an unreadable
.B \-\-debian\-keyring
file. Everything was restored.
.TP
.B 4
A failure after packages started changing. Run the program again with
.B \-\-resume \-\-yes
and the same mirror options to finish.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/regolith-convert-to-debian/state
Record of a conversion that stopped partway.
.TP
.I /var/backups/regolith-convert-to-debian/apt
Copy of
.I /etc/apt
from before the conversion.
.SH NOTES
Run the conversion from a text console rather than from the graphical session
it replaces. The boot loader is not changed beyond what the Debian kernel
packages do themselves; check that the Debian kernel boots before removing
the old one.
